      "source": "derived",
      "grading": "ungraded",
      "parts": [],
      "displayAnswer": "The first expression compared with the second is: a) >; b) <; c) <; d) >; e) =; f) =; g) >; h) =; i) <; j) <. All compared expressions are nonnegative, so comparison of their squares is equivalent.",
      "tasks": [
        {"label": "a", "input": "3\\sqrt3 versus \\sqrt{12}", "answer": "3\\sqrt3>\\sqrt{12}", "relation": ">", "squares": ["27", "12"], "reason": "Both are positive; 27>12. Equivalently 3sqrt(3)>2sqrt(3)."},
        {"label": "b", "input": "\\sqrt{20} versus 3\\sqrt5", "answer": "\\sqrt{20}<3\\sqrt5", "relation": "<", "squares": ["20", "45"], "reason": "20<45; equivalently 2sqrt(5)<3sqrt(5)."},
        {"label": "c", "input": "2\\sqrt3 versus 3\\sqrt2", "answer": "2\\sqrt3<3\\sqrt2", "relation": "<", "squares": ["12", "18"], "reason": "12<18."},
        {"label": "d", "input": "5\\sqrt4 versus 4\\sqrt5", "answer": "5\\sqrt4>4\\sqrt5", "relation": ">", "squares": ["100", "80"], "reason": "The first expression is 10 and both are positive; 100>80."},
        {"label": "e", "input": "\\frac13\\sqrt{54} versus \\frac15\\sqrt{150}", "answer": "\\frac13\\sqrt{54}=\\frac15\\sqrt{150}", "relation": "=", "squares": ["6", "6"], "reason": "54/9=150/25=6. Both expressions equal sqrt(6), not merely equal in magnitude."},
        {"label": "f", "input": "3\\sqrt{120} versus 2\\sqrt{270}", "answer": "3\\sqrt{120}=2\\sqrt{270}", "relation": "=", "squares": ["1080", "1080"], "reason": "9*120=4*270=1080; both expressions equal 6sqrt(30)."},
        {"label": "g", "input": "\\sqrt{72} versus 0.5\\sqrt{162}", "answer": "\\sqrt{72}>0.5\\sqrt{162}", "relation": ">", "squares": ["72", "81/2"], "reason": "0.5^2*162=162/4=81/2; 72>81/2. Equivalently 6sqrt(2)>(9/2)sqrt(2)."},
        {"label": "h", "input": "\\sqrt{24} versus \\frac13\\sqrt{216}", "answer": "\\sqrt{24}=\\frac13\\sqrt{216}", "relation": "=", "squares": ["24", "24"], "reason": "216/9=24; both expressions equal 2sqrt(6)."},
        {"label": "i", "input": "\\frac12\\sqrt6 versus 6\\sqrt{\\frac12}", "answer": "\\frac12\\sqrt6<6\\sqrt{\\frac12}", "relation": "<", "squares": ["3/2", "18"], "reason": "6/4=3/2 while 36/2=18; 3/2<18."},
        {"label": "j", "input": "\\frac23\\sqrt{72} versus 7\\sqrt{\\frac23}", "answer": "\\frac23\\sqrt{72}<7\\sqrt{\\frac23}", "relation": "<", "squares": ["32", "98/3"], "reason": "(4/9)*72=32=96/3; 49*(2/3)=98/3, and 96/3<98/3."}
      ]
