        {"label": "b", "input": "\\sqrt{10y^2}", "answer": "-y\\sqrt{10}", "domain": "y<0", "reason": "sqrt(y^2)=|y|=-y for y<0; -y is positive, as a principal square root must be."},
        {"label": "c", "input": "\\sqrt{16x^3}", "answer": "4x\\sqrt{x}", "domain": "x>0", "reason": "16x^3=(4x)^2*x. Since x>0, |4x|=4x and sqrt(x) is real."},
        {"label": "d", "input": "\\sqrt{0.01b^5}", "answer": "0.1b^2\\sqrt{b}", "domain": "b\\geq0", "reason": "0.01b^5=(0.1b^2)^2*b. The extracted factor 0.1b^2 is nonnegative and b>=0 makes the remaining root real; b=0 is included."},
        {"label": "e", "input": "\\sqrt{50a^7}", "answer": "5a^3\\sqrt{2a}", "domain": "a>0", "reason": "50a^7=(5a^3)^2*(2a); a>0 gives |5a^3|=5a^3 and 2a>0."},
        {"label": "f", "input": "\\sqrt{27c^6}", "answer": "-3c^3\\sqrt3", "domain": "c<0", "reason": "27c^6=(3c^3)^2*3. Since c<0 implies c^3<0, |3c^3|=-3c^3. The final quantity is positive, not the negative 3c^3sqrt(3)."}
      ]
