        {"label": "c", "input": "x\\sqrt{2/x}", "answer": "\\sqrt{2x}", "domain": "x\\in(0,\\infty)", "reason": "The denominator requires x!=0 and 2/x>=0 forces x>0. Thus x is a positive insertable factor and x^2*(2/x)=2x. The equality is only on the original x>0 domain, not at x=0."},
        {"label": "d", "input": "x\\sqrt{-2/x}", "answer": "-\\sqrt{-2x}", "domain": "x\\in(-\\infty,0)", "reason": "x!=0 and -2/x>=0 force x<0. Write x=-|x|, insert |x|^2=x^2, and retain the minus: -sqrt(x^2*(-2/x))=-sqrt(-2x). Zero is still excluded."}
