      "table_status": "HOLD-exact-table-preprocessing-and-value-provenance",
      "displayAnswer": "Method 1 mathematically evaluates 6\\sqrt{0.3333} = 3\\sqrt{3333}/50, approximately 3.463928405727. Method 2 uses the exact identity 6\\sqrt{1/3}=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt3, approximately 3.464101615138. Method 2 is algebraically more convenient: no truncation of 1/3 and no post-lookup multiplication. The actual table readings, table preprocessing, rounding and table-specific convenience comparison remain HOLD; the decimal numbers here are mathematical references only, NOT readings from any table.",
      "tasks": [
        {"label": "1", "input": "Look up sqrt(0.3333), then multiply by 6", "answer": "6\\sqrt{0.3333}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{3333}}{50}", "mathematical_reference": "3.463928405727", "reason": "0.3333=3333/10000 exactly, so sqrt(0.3333)=sqrt(3333)/100. The requested method returns 6 times this value. Because 1/3-0.3333=1/30000, it already has a radicand-truncation error before any table rounding.", "table_route_id": "829-1", "table_status": "HOLD"},
        {"label": "2", "input": "Rewrite 6sqrt(1/3) as sqrt(12) and look it up", "answer": "\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt3", "mathematical_reference": "3.464101615138", "reason": "6>=0, so 6sqrt(1/3)=sqrt(6^2/3)=sqrt(12) exactly. Unlike method 1, the radicand is not a decimal approximation to 1/3.", "table_route_id": "829-2", "table_status": "HOLD"},
        {"label": "comparison", "input": "Which of the two methods is more convenient?", "answer": "Method 2 is algebraically preferable; its actual table lookup convenience is conditional on the source table's available entries and instructions.", "reason": "An exact rewrite gives an integer radicand 12 and removes the multiplication after the root lookup. Method 1 gives a smaller exact result: its square is 11.9988, not 12. The exact difference is 0.0012/(sqrt(12)+sqrt(11.9988)), approximately 0.000173209411 before table error. If a table reading has error e, method 1 multiplies that root error by 6. Specific row, correction and rounding advantages cannot be claimed until the parent establishes the table.", "table_specific_convenience_status": "HOLD"}
      ]
    },
