      "table_status": "HOLD-for-radius-lookups-only",
      "displayAnswer": "The radius is r=\\sqrt{S/\\pi}, not plus/minus that root, because a radius is nonnegative. With the prescribed approximate pi=3.14, a) r approximately sqrt(625/157) cm, mathematical reference 1.995217211169 cm; b) r approximately sqrt(412/157) cm, mathematical reference 1.619939449997 cm. The source-table preprocessing and readings remain HOLD; these decimals are NOT table readings. Increasing area to 4 times its original value doubles the radius. Reducing area to 1/25 of its original value makes the radius 1/5 of its original value.",
      "tasks": [
        {"label": "inverse", "input": "Express r in terms of S in S=pi*r^2", "answer": "r=\\sqrt{S/\\pi}", "domain": "\\pi>0, S\\geq0, r\\geq0; a nondegenerate circle has S>0 and r>0", "reason": "Divide by pi>0 to get r^2=S/pi. Algebra gives two signed roots for S>0, but the geometric radius retains only the nonnegative root. S=0 permits r=0 only as a degenerate extension; S<0 has no real radius."},
        {"label": "a", "input": "S approximately 12.5 cm^2, pi approximately 3.14", "answer": "r\\approx\\sqrt{625/157}\\,\\mathrm{cm}", "mathematical_reference_cm": "1.995217211169", "reason": "Using the prescribed approximate inputs as a computational model, 12.5/3.14=(25/2)/(157/50)=625/157, approximately 3.980891719745. Its positive square root is approximately 1.995217211169 cm. This exact rational computation of the approximate-input model is not an exact physical radius or a table reading.", "table_route_id": "831-a", "table_status": "HOLD"},
        {"label": "b", "input": "S approximately 8.24 cm^2, pi approximately 3.14", "answer": "r\\approx\\sqrt{412/157}\\,\\mathrm{cm}", "mathematical_reference_cm": "1.619939449997", "reason": "8.24/3.14=(206/25)/(157/50)=412/157, approximately 2.624203821656. The nonnegative root is approximately 1.619939449997 cm. Retain division precision until the real table's preprocessing is known; do not assume that a rounded radicand has been supplied by the text.", "table_route_id": "831-b", "table_status": "HOLD"},
        {"label": "scale-4", "input": "Area becomes 4 times its original value", "answer": "r_{new}=2r_{old}", "reason": "At fixed positive pi, sqrt(4S/pi)=2sqrt(S/pi). The radius doubles, not quadruples; no table is needed."},
        {"label": "scale-1/25", "input": "Area becomes 1/25 of its original value", "answer": "r_{new}=r_{old}/5", "reason": "sqrt(S/(25pi))=(1/5)sqrt(S/pi). The radius becomes one fifth, not one twenty-fifth; no table is needed."}
      ]
